    <briefdescription>
<para>Detects quality divergence and hallucination signals in the reflection trace, halting the cycle before errors are amplified. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Two detection mechanisms:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Marker detection</bold> – Scans response and critique text for phrases that indicate the model is self-correcting fabricated content (e.g. &quot;I was
   wrong&quot;, &quot;my previous response was incorrect&quot;).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Divergence detection</bold> – Monitors the quality trajectory; halts if the rolling average of the last <computeroutput>window_</computeroutput> steps drops more than <computeroutput>divergence_threshold_</computeroutput> below the preceding step&apos;s score.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para>Golem.de (2026-03): &quot;Reflection Tuning bei KI: Selbstkritik bis hin
     zur Halluzination&quot; — empirical motivation <ref refid="bench__rewrite__engine_8cpp_1abe0af0d1fcf2406ab923ca4fb438b343" kindref="member">for</ref> this guard. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
